# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/herbalism-alchemy
title Herbalism + Alchemy 1-300
category Professions
kind profession
skills Herbalism, Alchemy
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Herbalism and Alchemy 1-300 together, for both factions: each Alchemy stretch starts with a
# Herbalism loop sized to what that stretch needs, which also raises Herbalism, and the craft
# follows with the materials in your bags. Spares carry to the next stretch, and when a stretch
# needs what Herbalism cannot gather yet, Herbalism catches up first. Herbalism ranks are trained at
# the Alchemy trainer visit when the skill allows. Herbalism reaches 300 before the last Alchemy
# stretch.
#
# The Herbalism loops are the Herbalism guide's (densest ground at a safe level, picked where you
# are); the Alchemy route, its recipes, trainers, vendor goods and counts the Alchemy guide's
# (enough for 9 players in 10). Anything Herbalism does not give is bought or farmed as there
# (Gather, Buy or Mix).
#
# ASSUMED: how far Herbalism rises on a stretch's materials is the Herbalism guide's expected
# skill-ups per node on the band's loops and what players' recorded gathers gave per node, averaged
# over the band's loops.
# About 10 hours of herbalism in 23 gathering stretches; it gathers about 200 Bruiseweed, 150
# Silverleaf, 130 Mageroyal, 120 Peacebloom, 110 Stranglekelp and 110 Briarthorn.
#
# Alchemy brews potions, elixirs and oils from herbs and vials. Herbalism is its partner: nearly
# every herb on this route is one you can pick yourself; the vials come from alchemy and trade
# supply vendors, and two fish from the Auction House.
#
# Ranks: Apprentice at any level from any Alchemy trainer (the first trainer teaches recipes only up
# to 50); Journeyman from level 10 at the city trainers; Expert from level 20 (50s) at Doctor
# Herbert Halsey in Undercity, Ainethil in Darnassus or Master Mycologist Shurome in Felwood's
# Emerald Sanctuary; Artisan from level 35 at Rogvar in Stonard, Kylanna Windwhisper in Feathermoon
# Stronghold or Shurome.
#
# Two recipes on the route come from vendors: Nature Protection Potion (Alchemist Pestlezugg in
# Tanaris, Glyx Brewright in Booty Bay) and the Elixir of Superior Defense recipe, which teaches the
# Elixir of Greater Defense (Kor'geld in Orgrimmar, Soolie Berryfizz in Ironforge). The transmutes
# and the Philosopher's Stone they need are not on this route: they give a point an hour at most.
#
# The route (crafts are about what it takes; yellow and green recipes can take a few more):
# Apprentice (1-55), from level 1:
#    1-10  9 Elixir of Minor Force: 9 Silverleaf, 9 Empty Vial
#   10-55  45 Elixir of Minor Defense: 45 Silverleaf, 45 Peacebloom, 45 Empty Vial
# Journeyman (55-150), from level 10:
#   55-65  10 Minor Mana Potion: 10 Mageroyal, 10 Peacebloom, 10 Empty Vial
#   65-90  28 Elixir of Minor Fortitude: 28 Peacebloom, 56 Earthroot, 28 Empty Vial
#   90-120 30 Elixir of Wisdom: 30 Mageroyal, 60 Briarthorn, 30 Empty Vial
#  120-130 10 Lesser Mana Potion: 10 Mageroyal, 10 Empty Vial, 10 Stranglekelp
#  130-150 20 Fire Oil: 20 Empty Vial, 40 Firefin Snapper
# Expert (150-225), from level 20:
#  150-165 15 Elixir of Fire Power: 15 Kingsblood, 15 Leaded Vial, 30 Fire Oil
#  165-195 36 Mana Potion: 36 Kingsblood, 36 Leaded Vial, 36 Stranglekelp
#  195-225 36 Nature Protection Potion: 36 Liferoot, 36 Leaded Vial, 36 Stranglekelp
# Artisan (225-300), from level 35:
#  225-235 26 Nature Protection Potion: 26 Liferoot, 26 Leaded Vial, 26 Stranglekelp
#  235-250 15 Elixir of Greater Intellect: 15 Khadgar's Whisker, 15 Blindweed, 15 Crystal Vial
#  250-260 47 Stonescale Oil: 47 Leaded Vial, 47 Stonescale Eel
#  260-265 10 Elixir of Greater Intellect: 10 Khadgar's Whisker, 10 Blindweed, 10 Crystal Vial
#  265-300 44 Elixir of Greater Defense: 44 Sungrass, 44 Crystal Vial, 88 Stonescale Oil

